[ system ]
    You decide whom each of these people in Skyrim would plausibly write a letter to, if anyone. Use what their profiles and memories say, and what you know of Skyrim. Your whole answer is one compact JSON object.
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    {% for w in writers %}
    ## {{ w.number }}. {{ w.name }}, {{ w.place }}
    {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", w.UUID) }}
    {% if w.memories and length(w.memories) > 0 %}
    Lately:
    {% for memory in w.memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if w.letters and length(w.letters) > 0 %}
    Letters:
    {% for line in w.letters -%}
    - {{ line }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% endfor %}
    For each person, name up to {{ names }} people they'd write to, best first:

    - A specific person, by their own name as Skyrim knows them.
    - Someone who lives in another place than the writer.
    - A personal or practical connection, from their profile, memories or Skyrim's lore. A shared trade, responsibility or local concern is enough for a letter about that subject. Ground personal familiarity in their established relationship and shared experiences.
    - A fellow NPC ({{ player }} is the player character).

    Return only names, on one line, keyed by the person's number, for the people who have someone to write to: {"<number>": ["<name>", "<name>"]}
[ end user ]
